        <id>link-a0502bf3fa360b6a88fd7b232ecf1f94</id>
        <link href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48490024"/>
        <updated>2026-06-12T03:59:47.993Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<div class="Story_container"><div class="Story_data"><div class="Story_title"><a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48490024"><span>Show HN: Homebrew 6.0.0</span></a><a href="https://brew.sh/2026/06/11/homebrew-6.0.0/" target="_blank" class="Story_link">(https://brew.sh/2026/06/11/homebrew-6.0.0/)</a></div><div class="Story_meta"><span><a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48490024">1472 points</a></span><span class="Story_separator">|</span><span><a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=mikemcquaid"><span>mikemcquaid</span></a></span><span class="Story_separator">|</span><span><a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48490024">5 days ago</a></span><span class="Story_separator">|</span><span><a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48490024">361 comments</a></span><div class="Story_comment"><span>Today, I’m proud to announce Homebrew 6.0.0. The most significant changes since 5.1.0 are a new tap trust security mechanism, the new faster, smaller, default internal Homebrew JSON API, sandboxing on Linux, better defaults informed by our user survey, many brew bundle improvements, improved performance and initial support for macOS 27 (Golden Gate).<p>Happy to discuss any questions here!</p></span></div></div></div></div>]]></content>
